 "circuits": [],
 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Four glass-passivated junctions form a full-wave bridge: AC goes across the two ~ leads, rectified current leaves at + and returns at -. Forward voltage, leakage, capacitance and surge figures are per diode."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Current derating",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "On a glass-epoxy board the average output holds 0.5 A up to about 35 °C ambient, then falls in a straight line to zero near 150 °C. On a 20 mm square aluminium substrate it holds 0.8 A up to about 30 °C and falls to zero at the same end point. Both lines apply to resistive or inductive loads."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Surge",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The 35 A figure is one 8.3 ms half-sine (60 Hz) on top of rated load. Repeated half-cycles at 40 °C ambient lower the allowed peak: at 60 Hz about 19 A for 12 cycles and 9 A for 100; at 50 Hz it starts at 30 A for one cycle and is about 6 A at 100."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Thermal",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Junction-to-ambient resistance is 85 °C/W on the glass-epoxy board and 70 °C/W on the aluminium substrate; junction-to-lead is 20 °C/W."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Assembly and compliance",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Moisture sensitivity level 1 to J-STD-020, with a 260 °C peak for lead-free reflow. Leads are matte tin, solderable to J-STD-002 and JESD22-B102. The mold compound is rated UL 94 V-0, and the part is UL recognised under file E54214. Polarity is marked on the body."
  }
 ],
